{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1146481-superhero-and-supervillain-names","id":1146481,"title":"Superhero (and Supervillain) Names","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-03T16:34:27-07:00","id":1146481,"title":"Superhero (and Supervillain) Names","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1130544-changeling-kickstarter-pushed-back-to-2018-no-it-s-2017?p=1146386#post1146386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's not, like, <i>Crisis of Infinite Darkness</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am inspired. Quick, I want superhero (and let's be honest, supervillain for some) names for each splat/organization combo. Yes, given the amount of combinations and differing tastes, this will literally be an endless task, but by Arcadia's foulest depths it will be fun. Fair warning, I suck at names, but I make up for it with enthusiasm!<br /> <br /> <br /> Fire-Touched Pure: Sickness<br /> <br /> Summer Court Ogre Stonebones: Stonebones (realizing the kiths are already awesome supernames.)<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul Gangrel (no bloodline): Science Beast<br /> <br /> And go!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 10-03-2017, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T16:57:38-07:00","id":1146487,"title":"","content":"I had an Obrimos Libertine who used his Shadow Name, &quot;Silver Fire&quot; as a nom de guerre in that way. In fact, Shadow Names seem like they're perfect for use as superhero/villain codenames.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T17:36:57-07:00","id":1146497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1146481-superhero-and-supervillain-names?p=1146487#post1146487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an Obrimos Libertine who used his Shadow Name, &quot;Silver Fire&quot; as a nom de guerre in that way. In fact, Shadow Names seem like they're perfect for use as superhero/villain codenames.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Was he styled as &quot;Silverfire&quot; or &quot;The Silver Fire&quot; or &quot;Silverfire Man&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T17:59:12-07:00","id":1146503,"title":"","content":"You might check out the Night Horrors books. They usually introduce character with a nickname that could work in a comic world. Of course most lines have nicknames for their characters, be it deed names in Werewolf or Shadow Names in Mage to give you a good head start.<br /> <br /> Here's various werewolf entries from Wolfsbane, usually along with their pack.<br /> <br /> Saint Anthony's Fire. Tox-Never-Speaks, Master of Strychnine. Father Strict, Master of Hemotoxin. Doc, Master of Hemlock.<br /> <br /> The Caretaker. Mama Vigil. Found. Big Bob.<br /> <br /> Bloody Mary. Typhoid Mary. Father Wolf. Grim Root.<br /> <br /> The Silver Hook, Johnny Shadow. The Skinner King. Brother of Fire.<br /> <br /> Dar-us. The Slow Killer. Bone Grinder. Kul Thari (it means Endless Moment of Death).<br /> <br /> The Cleansing Flame. Rabid Sister. Defies the Moon. Walks with Fury.<br /> <br /> Twisted Mirror. Desolation Jess.<br /> <br /> Officer Death. The Grim Trooper. Seething Brave.<br /> <br /> The Wolf-Born. Bringer of Ruin. Flesh-Ripper. Burning Whisper. Prey-Render.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-03-2017, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T18:15:50-07:00","id":1146510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1146481-superhero-and-supervillain-names?p=1146497#post1146497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Was he styled as &quot;Silverfire&quot; or &quot;The Silver Fire&quot; or &quot;Silverfire Man&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Silver Fire.&quot; To elaborate, the fire in his name is intended to be the flames of justice. Technically, his Shadow Name was &quot;The Everburning Silver Fire,&quot; but that's a little bit of a mouthful. He explicitly set out to become a superhero, because he was a nerdy teenager who found out that he has superpowers, so of course he did. He was the joke of the group right up until a Strix assault, when it turned out he was the main Forces mage in the group. He earned his name that night.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T18:21:03-07:00","id":1146513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1146481-superhero-and-supervillain-names?p=1146510#post1146510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;The Silver Fire.&quot; To elaborate, the fire in his name is intended to be the flames of justice. Technically, his Shadow Name was &quot;The Everburning Silver Fire,&quot; but that's a little bit of a mouthful. He explicitly set out to become a superhero, because he was a nerdy teenager who found out that he has superpowers, so of course he did. He was the joke of the group right up until a Strix assault, when it turned out he was the main Forces mage in the group. He earned his name that night.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;The flames of justice&quot;? delightfully cheesy. I love it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T18:23:43-07:00","id":1146514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1146481-superhero-and-supervillain-names?p=1146503#post1146503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might check out the Night Horrors books. They usually introduce character with a nickname that could work in a comic world. Of course most lines have nicknames for their characters, be it deed names in Werewolf or Shadow Names in Mage to give you a good head start.<br /> <br /> Here's various werewolf entries from Wolfsbane, usually along with their pack.<br /> <br /> Saint Anthony's Fire. Tox-Never-Speaks, Master of Strychnine. Father Strict, Master of Hemotoxin. Doc, Master of Hemlock.<br /> <br /> The Caretaker. Mama Vigil. Found. Big Bob.<br /> <br /> Bloody Mary. Typhoid Mary. Father Wolf. Grim Root.<br /> <br /> The Silver Hook, Johnny Shadow. The Skinner King. Brother of Fire.<br /> <br /> Dar-us. The Slow Killer. Bone Grinder. Kul Thari (it means Endless Moment of Death).<br /> <br /> The Cleansing Flame. Rabid Sister. Defies the Moon. Walks with Fury.<br /> <br /> Twisted Mirror. Desolation Jess.<br /> <br /> Officer Death. The Grim Trooper. Seething Brave.<br /> <br /> The Wolf-Born. Bringer of Ruin. Flesh-Ripper. Burning Whisper. Prey-Render.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those are good villain/90s antihero names. But I'm more interested in what people on the forums come up with.<br /> <br /> That said, Desolation Jess, The Caretaker and Officer Death are great names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T04:06:53-07:00","id":1146609,"title":"","content":"Nemesis Beasts: Nemesis, Punisher, Judges<br /> <br /> My aspiring-to-be-a-hero Tammuz earned his 'hero' nickname as &quot;The Breaker&quot;. Being a Titan that has just a beginning Grasp of concepts like intention, The Merciless torment, Falling Into torment, Starting A gangwar and &quot;solving&quot; crime with unrestrained force will do that. After all, ripping out an arm means that arm will no longer steal, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T05:20:17-07:00","id":1146629,"title":"","content":"*grins* I love this thread already","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T06:40:22-07:00","id":1146649,"title":"","content":"Ex-Knight of St George turned Yuri's Group security: Cathexis<br /> <br /> Panopticon archemesis of the above: Sublimation<br /> <br /> (Yeah, they have a very psychological thems to them).<br /> <br /> And of course,<br /> <br /> British Autumn Court Darkling: Batfellow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"